   {
    "quote": "1. **Trace to the birth certificate:** follow each citation to its citation until the original appears — the survey, the paper, the filing, the dataset. The questions at the origin: who made it, with what method, what sample, when, and *with what incentive* (vendor research isn't wrong by default, but its selection pressure is part of the record).",
    "url": "https://skillmd.com/skills/mohitagw15856/source-triangulation",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "2. **Independence is methods, not mastheads:** two outlets citing the same study = one source; a survey and a separate dataset agreeing = two. The echo test: do the supporting sources share numbers verbatim? Identical figures across \"independent\" sources is the fingerprint of a single origin echoing.",
    "url": "https://skillmd.com/skills/mohitagw15856/source-triangulation",
    "pass": 3,
